In article <893@devnull.mpd.tandem.com> dwelch@devnull.mpd.tandem.com (Dan Welch) writes:
>I have a problem, though:  when my character (or a monster) throws
>something, I get a lot of excess characters showing up,  I get a lot
>of )s or whatever I am throwing, mixed in with some 5s.  Before I
>begin digging my fingers through all umpteen thousand lines of code,
>has anyone else seen this?  Is there an easy answer?  I haven't been
>able to find any documentation of this problem.  My apologies if this
>is a hacked-to-death (ahem) problem.

The problem is, that the 'delay time' in the termcap entry is not honored
as such.  Whether this is a programming error or not I don't know, but
I solved on my system by deleting de 'delay time' in my favourite termcap
entries.  See the termcap(5) manual page for more.  Or ask me, if you
don't understand this short technical answer.

